      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As expected,\n\nEAC killed community of QoL and open-source non-malicious mods,\n\nbut malicious guys are still there.\n\nHackers just found other ways to hook and preload code to bypass EAC,\n\nand selling their mod clients through shade dealers like drugs.\n\nThat happened very soon after EAC was enforced, and for 2+ years they periodically finding vulnerabilities by reversing il2cpp and exploiting them.\n\n🫠🫠🫠\n\nDevs must understand that EAC is not magical cure from all issues, and client should always assumed to be un-trusted. Those 2+ years has shown that just only EAC is not enough.",
